module test.claim.runner.runner_user_session_label_witness

// THE CLAIM: the user-session label is granted by a PARSED CONVERGE RECEIPT about that host, and by
// nothing else.
//
// gunbc.runner.runner_host_deploy runner_job_user_session_hosts is the ROSTER (the converge's input
// population), and gunbc.runner.runner_user_session_receipt RunnerUserSessionConvergeReceipt is the
// EVIDENCE -- the three readings a converge run reported for one host, parsed from the document that run
// wrote. The composition (gunbc.runner.runner_registration_labels
// runner_evidence_gated_registration_labels) grants the label only when the host is rostered
// AND the supplied receipt parses, is ABOUT that host, and every reading in it holds. There is no receipt
// data in-tree (reviews 87051/87054/87126/87136/87155: hand-copied rows are DESIGN 6's transcribed
// output, and a row cannot re-read a host): production supplies ReceiptAbsent until the follow-up named
// in the PR body of gunbc#15253 wires the fleet-converge leg to run the receipt read
// (runner_user_session_converge_receipt_read_argv) and parse the bytes. THE LABEL IS OFF IN PRODUCTION
// WHILE THAT IS TRUE, and the controls below prove the grant turns it on ONLY from a parsed receipt --
// every receipt a control uses is a document the control PARSER-READY BUILT by writing the bytes through
// parse_runner_user_session_converge_receipt, so no control hands the grant a receipt the reader could
// not produce.
//
// The controls drive each channel a label could reach the registration through, rather than restating
// the grant:
//   1. THE GRANT'S TYPED STATES -- rostered+parsed+holding Granted; rostered+absent,
//      rostered+unparsable-bytes, rostered+holding-a-named-reading-failure, and a receipt about another
//      host all RosteredUnconverged with the CAUSE carried; unrostered+receipt ReceiptedUnrostered;
//      unrostered+nothing Unadmitted. A forged roster and a forged receipt are both parameters.
//   2. THE PARSER ITSELF -- the bytes a converge run writes parse to the readings the converge took;
//      bytes that are not the document do not parse to a guess. This is the control that makes "the gate
//      reads the receipt" mean something: the grant consumes the parser's output, so a parser that
//      fabricated readings from garbage would put the label on the host.
//   3. THE GATE IN PRODUCTION SHAPE -- the production entry passes no receipt, so srv4 is
//      RosteredUnconverged and carries NO label; only the receipt-parameterized composition entry puts
//      the label on srv4's registration. (The fleet read is the follow-up; the label being off at the
//      production entry is the honest state, so the control asserts exactly that.)
//   4. THE CLASS-ARGUMENT CHANNEL -- runner_registration_labels_of_class takes class_labels from its
//      caller, so a forged argument must not be able to grant the label.
//   5. THE HOST-SPELLABLE PLATFORM HALF -- the composition strips the label from the offer-derived half
//      before re-adding it from the gate.
//   6. THE SLOT GRAIN -- the CI slot follows its host's evidence, and the deploy slot (a different
//      principal) does not inherit the host's capability even when a receipt is handed to the entry.
//   7. THE CONSUMER -- the label's consumer is the runs-on selector of the jobs that run a command under
//      the job account's user manager: gunbc#14972's credential-acquisition rows, the pool the roster is
//      waiting on (DESIGN 3c: the frontier is recorded beside the row, in gunbc.runner.runner_host_deploy
//      runner_job_user_session_hosts). The control builds the selector the way the emitter builds a
//      host-pinned CI spec and checks satisfaction against what each registration advertises, with and
//      without a receipt.
//   8. THE READ SPEC -- the reader runs cat of a path; a spec that runs another program or drops the path
//      is a different document.
//
// A REFUSAL IS NOT AN ABSENCE, AND NO HELPER HIDES ONE. There is no labels_of with a Refused => []
// default: every control matches the RunnerRegistrationLabelsResolution directly, so a host whose facts
// stopped resolving makes that control FALSE rather than vacuously green (reviews 86935 and 87051;
// DESIGN 5: "no plausible output is fabricated" -- a folded-in empty list is exactly the fabricated
// default a later control would inherit).

